  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0070_0dad67cbf988.png\" style=\"width: 527px; height: 370px;\" /></p><p>The peptide is having N-terminal at left-hand side and C-terminal at right-hand side. During hydrolysis the bond breaks between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p><p>Hydrolysis of the given tetrapeptide will give the following:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0070_70fefab580ad.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 262px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0070_2303e926746c.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 238px;\" /></p>"
